-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 14: payment into and out of Court.  Part roc2, layer 1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT: see roc2-order-9a.l4 and NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (roc2)").
-- Every answer is subject to O 3 r 2(1) (roc1): the Court's discretion to order otherwise.
-- The count of a period is O 3 r 3 (roc1): a period function takes `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`.
-- An event limit ("before the trial or hearing begins", "before the Judge begins to deliver judgment") is a fact the asker states, not a date.
-- Order 44, Rule 11 is not in this part: r 3(6) takes its answer as an input (`Order 44 Rule 11 answers`).
-- Content-requirement functions ("the notice must state ... if it is the case") answer JUST TRUE when nothing is required (fork F-vac in NOTES.md).
-- Money is a NUMBER of Singapore dollars.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 14, Rule 1 -- payment into Court`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `o 14 r 1(1) what the payment is in satisfaction of` IS ONE OF
    `o 14 r 1(1) the cause of action in respect of which the claimant claims`
    `o 14 r 1(1) all of the causes of action joined in the action`
    `o 14 r 1(1) any of the causes of action joined in the action`

-- src:1343 | 1. —(1) In any action for a debt or damages, any defendant may at any time after the defendant has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action pay into Court a sum of money in satisfaction of the cause of action in respect of which the claimant claims or, where 2 or more causes of action are joined in the action, a sum or sums of money in satisfaction of all or any of those causes of action. (2) On making any payment into Court under this Rule, or on increasing any such payment already made, the defendant must give notice of the payment or further payment in Form 27 to the claimant and every other defendant (if any); and within 3 days after receiving the notice the claimant must send the defendant a written acknowledgment of its receipt.
@ref O 14 r 1(1) (src:1343)
GIVEN `the action is for a debt or damages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `two or more causes of action are joined in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      satisfaction IS A `o 14 r 1(1) what the payment is in satisfaction of`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 1(1) the defendant may pay a sum of money into Court` MEANS
    IF `the action is for a debt or damages`
    THEN
        IF `the defendant has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action`
        THEN
            CONSIDER satisfaction
            WHEN `o 14 r 1(1) the cause of action in respect of which the claimant claims` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `o 14 r 1(1) all of the causes of action joined in the action` THEN
                IF `two or more causes of action are joined in the action`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where 2 or more causes of action are joined in the action" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
            WHEN `o 14 r 1(1) any of the causes of action joined in the action` THEN
                IF `two or more causes of action are joined in the action`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where 2 or more causes of action are joined in the action" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time after the defendant has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05, (a): before the notice is filed is outside it, as in O 9 r 17(1)) [marginal-a]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any action for a debt or damages"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1343 | 1. —(1) In any action for a debt or damages, any defendant may at any time after the defendant has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action pay into Court a sum of money in satisfaction of the cause of action in respect of which the claimant claims or, where 2 or more causes of action are joined in the action, a sum or sums of money in satisfaction of all or any of those causes of action. (2) On making any payment into Court under this Rule, or on increasing any such payment already made, the defendant must give notice of the payment or further payment in Form 27 to the claimant and every other defendant (if any); and within 3 days after receiving the notice the claimant must send the defendant a written acknowledgment of its receipt.
@ref O 14 r 1(2) (src:1343)
