-- src:1343 | 1. —(1) In any action for a debt or damages, any defendant may at any time after the defendant has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action pay into Court a sum of money in satisfaction of the cause of action in respect of which the claimant claims or, where 2 or more causes of action are joined in the action, a sum or sums of money in satisfaction of all or any of those causes of action. (2) On making any payment into Court under this Rule, or on increasing any such payment already made, the defendant must give notice of the payment or further payment in Form 27 to the claimant and every other defendant (if any); and within 3 days after receiving the notice the claimant must send the defendant a written acknowledgment of its receipt.
@ref O 14 r 1(2) (src:1343)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 14 r 1(2) party` `o 14 r 1(2) act`
`o 14 r 1(2) the claimant must acknowledge the notice` MEANS
    PARTY `o 14 r 1(2) the claimant`
    MUST `o 14 r 1(2) send the defendant a written acknowledgment of the receipt`
    WITHIN 3
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 14 r 1(2) the claimant` BECAUSE "the written acknowledgment was not sent within 3 days after the claimant received the notice"

-- src:1344 | (3) A defendant may, without permission, give notice of an increase in a payment made under this Rule but, subject to that and without affecting paragraph (5), a notice of payment may not be withdrawn or amended without the permission of the Court which may be granted on such terms as may be just.
@ref O 14 r 1(3) (src:1344)
GIVEN `the notice is of an increase in a payment made under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 1(3) the defendant may give notice of an increase without permission` MEANS
    IF `the notice is of an increase in a payment made under this Rule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "notice of an increase in a payment made under this Rule"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1344 | (3) A defendant may, without permission, give notice of an increase in a payment made under this Rule but, subject to that and without affecting paragraph (5), a notice of payment may not be withdrawn or amended without the permission of the Court which may be granted on such terms as may be just.
@ref O 14 r 1(3) (src:1344)
GIVEN `the notice is of an increase in a payment made under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court orders the notice to be amended under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 1(3) a notice of payment may be withdrawn or amended` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the notice is of an increase in a payment made under this Rule`) AND (NOT `the Court has given permission`) AND (NOT `the Court orders the notice to be amended under paragraph (5)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to that and without affecting paragraph (5), a notice of payment may not be withdrawn or amended without the permission of the Court" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for a notice withdrawn or amended "without the permission of the Court", other than an increase or an amendment under paragraph (5); outside it paragraph (3) is silent [marginal-b]

-- src:1344 | (3) A defendant may, without permission, give notice of an increase in a payment made under this Rule but, subject to that and without affecting paragraph (5), a notice of payment may not be withdrawn or amended without the permission of the Court which may be granted on such terms as may be just.
@ref O 14 r 1(3) (src:1344)
GIVEN `an application is made for permission to withdraw or amend a notice of payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 1(3) the Court may grant permission on such terms as may be just` MEANS
    IF `an application is made for permission to withdraw or amend a notice of payment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the permission of the Court which may be granted on such terms as may be just"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- Paragraph (4): a content requirement on the notice of payment where 2 or more causes of action are joined and money is paid in respect of all, or some only, of them.
-- src:1345 | (4) Where 2 or more causes of action are joined in the action and money is paid into Court under this Rule in respect of all, or some only of, those causes of action, the notice of payment — ( a )
-- src:1346 | must state that the money is paid in respect of all those causes of action or (as the case may be) must specify the cause or causes of action in respect of which the payment is made; and
@ref O 14 r 1(4)(a) (src:1345-1346)
GIVEN `two or more causes of action are joined in the action and money is paid into Court in respect of all, or some only, of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money is paid in respect of all those causes of action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the money is paid in respect of all those causes of action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies the cause or causes of action in respect of which the payment is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 1(4)(a) the notice of payment states or specifies the causes of action` MEANS
    IF NOT `two or more causes of action are joined in the action and money is paid into Court in respect of all, or some only, of them`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- nothing is required where the paragraph's "Where" does not hold (fork F-vac in NOTES.md) [marginal-a]
    ELSE
        IF `the money is paid in respect of all those causes of action`
        THEN
            IF `the notice states that the money is paid in respect of all those causes of action`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notice of payment must state that the money is paid in respect of all those causes of action" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]
        ELSE
            IF `the notice specifies the cause or causes of action in respect of which the payment is made`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or (as the case may be) must specify the cause or causes of action in respect of which the payment is made" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1347 | ( b )
-- src:1348 | where the defendant makes separate payments in respect of each, or any 2 or more, of those causes of action, must specify the sum paid in respect of that cause of action or (as the case may be) those causes of action.
@ref O 14 r 1(4)(b) (src:1347-1348)
GIVEN `two or more causes of action are joined in the action and money is paid into Court in respect of all, or some only, of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant makes separate payments in respect of each, or any 2 or more, of those causes of action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies the sum paid in respect of that cause of action or those causes of action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 1(4)(b) the notice of payment specifies the sum paid in respect of each cause of action` MEANS
    IF NOT `two or more causes of action are joined in the action and money is paid into Court in respect of all, or some only, of them`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- nothing is required where the paragraph's "Where" does not hold (fork F-vac in NOTES.md) [marginal-a]
    ELSE
        IF NOT `the defendant makes separate payments in respect of each, or any 2 or more, of those causes of action`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- nothing is required where there are no separate payments: "where the defendant makes separate payments" [marginal-a]
        ELSE
            IF `the notice specifies the sum paid in respect of that cause of action or those causes of action`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must specify the sum paid in respect of that cause of action or (as the case may be) those causes of action" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1350 | (6) Where a cause of action under section 10 of the Civil Law Act and a cause of action under section 20 of that Act are joined in an action, with or without any other cause of action, the causes of action under those sections are, for the purpose of paragraph (5), to be treated as one cause of action.
@ref O 14 r 1(6) (src:1350)
GIVEN `the number of causes of action joined in the action` IS A NUMBER
      `a cause of action under section 10 of the Civil Law Act and a cause of action under section 20 of that Act are joined in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 14 r 1(6) the number of causes of action for the purpose of paragraph (5)` MEANS
    IF `a cause of action under section 10 of the Civil Law Act and a cause of action under section 20 of that Act are joined in the action`
    THEN `the number of causes of action joined in the action` MINUS 1
    ELSE `the number of causes of action joined in the action`

-- src:1349 | (5) Where a single sum of money is paid into Court under this Rule in respect of 2 or more causes of action, then, if it appears to the Court that the claimant is embarrassed by the payment, the Court may, subject to paragraph (6), order the defendant to amend the notice of payment so as to specify the sum paid in respect of each cause of action.
@ref O 14 r 1(5) (src:1349)
GIVEN `a single sum of money is paid into Court under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of causes of action the sum is paid in respect of, counted as paragraph (6) requires` IS A NUMBER
      `it appears to the Court that the claimant is embarrassed by the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Rule 3(3) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 1(5) the Court may order the defendant to amend the notice of payment to specify the sum paid in respect of each cause of action` MEANS
    IF `Rule 3(3) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Rule 3(3) says "Rule 1(5) does not apply in relation to money paid into Court in an action after the trial or hearing of the action has begun"
    ELSE
        IF `a single sum of money is paid into Court under this Rule` AND `the number of causes of action the sum is paid in respect of, counted as paragraph (6) requires` AT LEAST 2 AND `it appears to the Court that the claimant is embarrassed by the payment`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a single sum of money is paid into Court under this Rule in respect of 2 or more causes of action, then, if it appears to the Court that the claimant is embarrassed by the payment" (a "where" and an "if" that fail) [marginal-a]

-- src:1350 | (6) Where a cause of action under section 10 of the Civil Law Act and a cause of action under section 20 of that Act are joined in an action, with or without any other cause of action, the causes of action under those sections are, for the purpose of paragraph (5), to be treated as one cause of action.
@ref O 14 r 1(6) (src:1350)
GIVEN `a cause of action under section 10 of the Civil Law Act and a cause of action under section 20 of that Act are joined in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
