`o 14 r 1(6) the causes of action are treated as one cause of action for the purpose of paragraph (5)` MEANS
    IF `a cause of action under section 10 of the Civil Law Act and a cause of action under section 20 of that Act are joined in the action`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a cause of action under section 10 of the Civil Law Act and a cause of action under section 20 of that Act are joined in an action" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b)) [marginal-a]

-- src:1351 | (7) For the purposes of this Rule, the claimant’s cause of action in respect of a debt or damages is to be construed as a cause of action in respect also of such interest as might be included in the judgment, if judgment were given at the date of the payment into Court.
@ref O 14 r 1(7) (src:1351)
GIVEN `the cause of action is the claimant's cause of action in respect of a debt or damages` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 1(7) the cause of action is construed as a cause of action in respect also of the interest that might be included in the judgment` MEANS
    IF `the cause of action is the claimant's cause of action in respect of a debt or damages`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the claimant's cause of action in respect of a debt or damages"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 14, Rule 2 -- payment in by defendant who has counterclaimed`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1353 | 2. Where a defendant, who makes by counterclaim a claim against the claimant for a debt or damages, pays a sum of money into Court under Rule 1, the notice of payment must state, if it be the case, that in making the payment the defendant has taken into account and intends to satisfy — ( a )
-- src:1354 | the cause of action in respect of which the defendant claims; or
-- src:1355 | ( b )
-- src:1356 | where 2 or more causes of action are joined in the counterclaim, all those causes of action or, if not all, which of them.
@ref O 14 r 2 (src:1353-1356)
GIVEN `the defendant makes by counterclaim a claim against the claimant for a debt or damages and pays a sum of money into Court under Rule 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in making the payment the defendant has taken into account and intends to satisfy the cause or causes of action in respect of which the defendant claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      `two or more causes of action are joined in the counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment takes into account all those causes of action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the payment takes into account and is intended to satisfy the cause or causes of action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies which of the causes of action are taken into account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 2 the notice of payment states what Rule 2 requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the defendant makes by counterclaim a claim against the claimant for a debt or damages and pays a sum of money into Court under Rule 1`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a defendant, who makes by counterclaim a claim against the claimant for a debt or damages, pays a sum of money into Court under Rule 1"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))
    ELSE
        IF NOT `in making the payment the defendant has taken into account and intends to satisfy the cause or causes of action in respect of which the defendant claims`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- nothing is required "if it be the case" is not the case (fork F-vac in NOTES.md) [marginal-a]
        ELSE
            IF `two or more causes of action are joined in the counterclaim` AND (NOT `the payment takes into account all those causes of action`)
            THEN
                IF `the notice specifies which of the causes of action are taken into account`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where 2 or more causes of action are joined in the counterclaim, all those causes of action or, if not all, which of them" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]
            ELSE
                IF `the notice states that the payment takes into account and is intended to satisfy the cause or causes of action`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notice of payment must state, if it be the case, that in making the payment the defendant has taken into account and intends to satisfy" (a) or (b) (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 14, Rule 3 -- acceptance of money paid into Court`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1358 | 3. —(1) Where money is paid into Court under Rule 1, then subject to paragraph (2), within 14 days after receipt of the notice of payment or, where more than one payment has been made or the notice has been amended, within 14 days after receipt of the notice of the last payment or the amended notice but, in any case, before the trial or hearing of the action begins, the claimant may — ( a )
@ref O 14 r 3(1) (src:1358)
`o 14 r 3(1) fourteen days after receipt of the notice of payment` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

DECLARE `o 14 r 3(1) what the claimant accepts` IS ONE OF
    `o 14 r 3(1)(a) the money paid in respect of the cause of action or all the causes of action in respect of which the claimant claims`
    `o 14 r 3(1)(b) the sum specified in the notice of payment in respect of some only of the causes of action`

-- The days are counted from receipt of the notice of the LAST payment or the amended notice (O 3 r 3 gives the last day).
-- src:1358 | 3. —(1) Where money is paid into Court under Rule 1, then subject to paragraph (2), within 14 days after receipt of the notice of payment or, where more than one payment has been made or the notice has been amended, within 14 days after receipt of the notice of the last payment or the amended notice but, in any case, before the trial or hearing of the action begins, the claimant may — ( a )
-- src:1359 | where the money was paid in respect of the cause of action or all the causes of action in respect of which the claimant claims, accept the money in satisfaction of that cause of action or those causes of action, as the case may be; or
-- src:1360 | ( b )
-- src:1361 | where the money was paid in respect of some only of the causes of action in respect of which the claimant claims, accept in satisfaction of any such cause or causes of action the sum specified in respect of that cause or those causes of action in the notice of payment,
-- src:1362 | by giving notice in Form 28 to every defendant to the action.
@ref O 14 r 3(1) (src:1358-1362)
GIVEN `money is paid into Court under Rule 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money was paid in respect of the cause of action or all the causes of action in respect of which the claimant claims` IS A BOOLEAN
      acceptance IS A `o 14 r 3(1) what the claimant accepts`
      `the date the claimant gives notice of acceptance` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the claimant gives the notice before the trial or hearing of the action begins` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is in Form 28 and is given to every defendant to the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 3(1) the claimant may accept the money` MEANS
    IF `money is paid into Court under Rule 1`
    THEN
        IF (acceptance EQUALS `o 14 r 3(1)(a) the money paid in respect of the cause of action or all the causes of action in respect of which the claimant claims` AND `the money was paid in respect of the cause of action or all the causes of action in respect of which the claimant claims`) OR (acceptance EQUALS `o 14 r 3(1)(b) the sum specified in the notice of payment in respect of some only of the causes of action` AND (NOT `the money was paid in respect of the cause of action or all the causes of action in respect of which the claimant claims`))
        THEN
            IF `the date the claimant gives notice of acceptance` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` AND `the claimant gives the notice before the trial or hearing of the action begins` AND `the notice is in Form 28 and is given to every defendant to the action`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after receipt of the notice of payment ... but in any case before the trial or hearing of the action begins, the claimant may ... by giving notice in Form 28 to every defendant to the action" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): (a) "where the money was paid in respect of the cause of action or all the causes of action" and (b) "where the money was paid in respect of some only of the causes of action" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where money is paid into Court under Rule 1" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1363 | (2) Where after the trial or hearing of an action has begun — ( a )
