      `the date the claimant accepts the money` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the claimant accepts before the Judge begins to deliver judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 3(2) the claimant may accept the money after the trial or hearing has begun` MEANS
    IF `money is paid into Court under Rule 1, or money in Court is increased by a further payment, after the trial or hearing of the action has begun`
    THEN
        IF `the date the claimant accepts the money` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` AND `the claimant accepts before the Judge begins to deliver judgment`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 2 days after receipt of the notice of payment or notice of the further payment ... but, in any case, before the Judge begins to deliver judgment" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where after the trial or hearing of an action has begun" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1368 | (3) Rule 1(5) does not apply in relation to money paid into Court in an action after the trial or hearing of the action has begun.
