    `o 14 r 3(4) another defendant sued jointly with or in the alternative to the defendant making the payment`
    `o 14 r 3(4) any other defendant`

-- src:1369 | (4) On the claimant accepting any money paid into Court, all further proceedings in the action or in respect of the specified cause or causes of action (as the case may be) to which the acceptance relates, both against the defendant making the payment and against any other defendant sued jointly with or in the alternative to the firstmentioned defendant are to be stayed.
@ref O 14 r 3(4) (src:1369)
GIVEN `the claimant accepts money paid into Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are those in the action or in respect of the specified cause or causes of action to which the acceptance relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      defendant IS A `o 14 r 3(4) a defendant`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 3(4) all further proceedings against the defendant are stayed` MEANS
    IF `the claimant accepts money paid into Court` AND `the proceedings are those in the action or in respect of the specified cause or causes of action to which the acceptance relates`
    THEN
        CONSIDER defendant
        WHEN `o 14 r 3(4) the defendant making the payment` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 14 r 3(4) another defendant sued jointly with or in the alternative to the defendant making the payment` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 14 r 3(4) any other defendant` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the stay is "against the defendant making the payment and against any other defendant sued jointly with or in the alternative to" that defendant
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the claimant accepting any money paid into Court, all further proceedings in the action or in respect of the specified cause or causes of action ... to which the acceptance relates are to be stayed" (a "on" that fails)

-- src:1370 | (5) Where money is paid into Court by a defendant who made a counterclaim and the notice of payment stated, in relation to any sum so paid, that in making the payment the defendant had taken into account and satisfied the cause or causes of action, or the specified cause or causes of action in respect of which the defendant claimed, then, on the claimant accepting that sum, all further proceedings on the counterclaim or in respect of the specified cause or causes of action (as the case may be) against the claimant are to be stayed.
@ref O 14 r 3(5) (src:1370)
GIVEN `money is paid into Court by a defendant who made a counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of payment stated, in relation to the sum, that in making the payment the defendant had taken into account and satisfied the cause or causes of action, or the specified cause or causes of action, in respect of which the defendant claimed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant accepts that sum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 3(5) all further proceedings on the counterclaim against the claimant are stayed` MEANS
    IF `money is paid into Court by a defendant who made a counterclaim` AND `the notice of payment stated, in relation to the sum, that in making the payment the defendant had taken into account and satisfied the cause or causes of action, or the specified cause or causes of action, in respect of which the defendant claimed` AND `the claimant accepts that sum`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where money is paid into Court by a defendant who made a counterclaim and the notice of payment stated ... then, on the claimant accepting that sum, all further proceedings on the counterclaim ... against the claimant are to be stayed" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1371 | (6) A claimant who has accepted any sum paid into Court is, subject to Rules 4 and 10 and Order 44, Rule 11, entitled to receive payment of that sum in satisfaction of the cause or causes of action to which the acceptance relates.
@ref O 14 r 3(6) (src:1371)
GIVEN `the claimant has accepted a sum paid into Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Rule 4 answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Rule 10 answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `Order 44 Rule 11 answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 3(6) the claimant is entitled to receive payment of the sum` MEANS
    IF `the claimant has accepted a sum paid into Court`
    THEN
        IF `Rule 4 answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `Rule 10 answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `Order 44 Rule 11 answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to Rules 4 and 10 and Order 44, Rule 11": one of them says no
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A claimant who has accepted any sum paid into Court"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

