§ `Order 14, Rules 4 and 5 -- payment out of money accepted; money remaining in Court`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1373 | 4. —(1) Where a claimant accepts any sum paid into Court and that sum was paid into Court — ( a )
-- src:1374 | by some but not all of the defendants sued jointly or in the alternative by the claimant;
-- src:1375 | ( b )
-- src:1376 | with a defence of tender before action; or
-- src:1377 | ( c )
-- src:1378 | in satisfaction either of causes of action arising under sections 10 and 20 of the Civil Law Act or of a cause of action arising under section 20 of that Act, where more than one person is entitled to the money,
-- src:1379 | the money in Court must not be paid out except under paragraph (2) or in pursuance of an order of the Court, and the order must deal with the whole costs of the action or of the cause of action to which the payment relates, as the case may be.
@ref O 14 r 4(1) (src:1373-1379)
GIVEN `the claimant accepts a sum paid into Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum was paid into Court by some but not all of the defendants sued jointly or in the alternative by the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum was paid into Court with a defence of tender before action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum was paid into Court in satisfaction of causes of action under sections 10 and 20 of the Civil Law Act or under section 20 of that Act, where more than one person is entitled to the money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money is paid out under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money is paid out in pursuance of an order of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 4(1) the money in Court may be paid out` MEANS
    IF `the claimant accepts a sum paid into Court` AND (`the sum was paid into Court by some but not all of the defendants sued jointly or in the alternative by the claimant` OR `the sum was paid into Court with a defence of tender before action` OR `the sum was paid into Court in satisfaction of causes of action under sections 10 and 20 of the Civil Law Act or under section 20 of that Act, where more than one person is entitled to the money`) AND (NOT `the money is paid out under paragraph (2)`) AND (NOT `the money is paid out in pursuance of an order of the Court`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the money in Court must not be paid out except under paragraph (2) or in pursuance of an order of the Court" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for a sum paid in as (a), (b) or (c) and accepted, "except under paragraph (2) or in pursuance of an order of the Court"; outside it paragraph (1) is silent [marginal-b]

-- src:1379 | the money in Court must not be paid out except under paragraph (2) or in pursuance of an order of the Court, and the order must deal with the whole costs of the action or of the cause of action to which the payment relates, as the case may be.
@ref O 14 r 4(1) (src:1379)
GIVEN `an order of the Court is made under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order deals with the whole costs of the action or of the cause of action to which the payment relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 4(1) the order deals with the whole costs` MEANS
    IF `an order of the Court is made under paragraph (1)`
    THEN
        IF `the order deals with the whole costs of the action or of the cause of action to which the payment relates`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the order must deal with the whole costs of the action or of the cause of action to which the payment relates, as the case may be" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the order"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1380 | (2) Where an order of the Court is required under paragraph (1) by reason only of paragraph (1)( a ), then, if, either before or after accepting the money paid into Court by some only of the defendants sued jointly or in the alternative by the claimant, the claimant discontinues the action against all other defendants and those defendants consent in writing to the payment out of that sum, it may be paid out without an order of the Court.
@ref O 14 r 4(2) (src:1380)
GIVEN `an order of the Court is required under paragraph (1) by reason only of paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant discontinues the action against all other defendants` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those defendants consent in writing to the payment out of that sum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 4(2) the money may be paid out without an order of the Court` MEANS
    IF `an order of the Court is required under paragraph (1) by reason only of paragraph (1)(a)` AND `the claimant discontinues the action against all other defendants` AND `those defendants consent in writing to the payment out of that sum`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "either before or after accepting the money": the time of discontinuance does not change the answer
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order of the Court is required under paragraph (1) by reason only of paragraph (1)(a), then, if ... the claimant discontinues the action against all other defendants and those defendants consent in writing" (a "where" or an "if" that fails) [marginal-a]

-- src:1381 | (3) Where after the trial or hearing of an action has begun, a claimant accepts any money paid into Court and all further proceedings in the action or in respect of the specified cause or causes of action (as the case may be) to which the acceptance relates are stayed by virtue of Rule 3(4) then, despite anything in paragraph (2), the money must not be paid out except in pursuance of an order of the Court, and the order must deal with the whole costs of the action.
