    IF `the trial or hearing of the action has begun` AND `the claimant accepts money paid into Court` AND `all further proceedings are stayed by virtue of Rule 3(4)` AND (NOT `the money is paid out in pursuance of an order of the Court`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "despite anything in paragraph (2), the money must not be paid out except in pursuance of an order of the Court" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for money accepted after the trial or hearing has begun and the proceedings stayed by Rule 3(4), "except in pursuance of an order of the Court"; outside it paragraph (3) is silent [marginal-b]

