    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the money remaining in Court must not be paid out except in pursuance of an order of the Court" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for money "not accepted in accordance with Rule 3", "except in pursuance of an order of the Court"; outside it Rule 5 is silent [marginal-b]

