      provision IS A `o 14 r 6 a provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 6 the provision applies accordingly with the necessary modifications` MEANS
    IF `the person is a claimant against whom a counterclaim is made or any other defendant to the counterclaim`
    THEN
        CONSIDER provision
        WHEN `o 14 r 6 Rule 1` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 14 r 6 Rule 3, except paragraph (5)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 14 r 6 Rule 3(5)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rules 3 (except paragraph (5))"
        WHEN `o 14 r 6 Rule 4` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 14 r 6 Rule 5` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 14 r 6 any other provision` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the Rule names Rules 1, 3 (except paragraph (5)), 4 and 5; it does not say that no other provision applies
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A claimant against whom a counterclaim is made and any other defendant to the counterclaim"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1387 | 7. Except in an action to which a defence of tender before action is pleaded, and except in an action all further proceedings in which are stayed by virtue of Rule 3(4) after the trial or hearing has begun, the fact that money has been paid into Court under Rules 1 to 6 must not be pleaded and no communication of that fact may be made to the Court at the trial or hearing of the action or counterclaim or of any question or issue as to the debt or damages until all questions of liability and of the amount of debt or damages have been decided.
@ref O 14 r 7 (src:1387)
GIVEN `a defence of tender before action is pleaded in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all further proceedings in the action are stayed by virtue of Rule 3(4) after the trial or hearing has begun` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all questions of liability and of the amount of debt or damages have been decided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 7 the fact that money has been paid into Court may be pleaded or communicated to the Court at the trial or hearing` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a defence of tender before action is pleaded in the action`) AND (NOT `all further proceedings in the action are stayed by virtue of Rule 3(4) after the trial or hearing has begun`) AND (NOT `all questions of liability and of the amount of debt or damages have been decided`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the fact that money has been paid into Court under Rules 1 to 6 must not be pleaded and no communication of that fact may be made to the Court at the trial or hearing ... until all questions of liability and of the amount of debt or damages have been decided" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition has two exceptions, an action with a defence of tender before action and an action stayed by Rule 3(4) after the trial has begun, and lasts only "until all questions of liability and of the amount of debt or damages have been decided"; outside it Rule 7 is silent [marginal-b]

-- src:1389 | 8. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2), money paid into Court under an order of the Court or a certificate of the Registrar must not be paid out except in pursuance of an order of the Court. (2) Unless the Court otherwise orders, a party who has paid money into Court pursuant to an order made under Order 9, Rule 17 — ( a )
