-- src:1391 | ( b )
-- src:1392 | if the party pleads a tender, may by that party’s pleading appropriate the whole or any part of the money as payment into Court of the money alleged to have been tendered,
-- src:1393 | and money appropriated in accordance with this Rule is deemed to be money paid into Court in accordance with Rule 1 or money paid into Court with a plea of tender (as the case may be), and this Order applies accordingly.
@ref O 14 r 8(2) (src:1389-1393)
GIVEN `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has paid money into Court pursuant to an order made under Order 9, Rule 17` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `o 14 r 8(2) how the money is appropriated`
      `the party pleads a tender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 8(2) the party may appropriate the money in this way` MEANS
    IF `the Court otherwise orders`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless the Court otherwise orders"; what the Court orders is for the order [marginal-b]
    ELSE
        IF `the party has paid money into Court pursuant to an order made under Order 9, Rule 17`
        THEN
            CONSIDER way
            WHEN `o 14 r 8(2)(a) by notice to the other party to a particular claim made in the originating claim or counterclaim and specified in the notice` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `o 14 r 8(2)(b) by the party's pleading, as payment into Court of the money alleged to have been tendered` THEN
                IF `the party pleads a tender`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the party pleads a tender" fails [marginal-a]
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a party who has paid money into Court pursuant to an order made under Order 9, Rule 17"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

DECLARE `o 14 r 8(2) how the appropriated money is deemed to have been paid in` IS ONE OF
    `o 14 r 8(2) money paid into Court in accordance with Rule 1`
    `o 14 r 8(2) money paid into Court with a plea of tender`

-- src:1393 | and money appropriated in accordance with this Rule is deemed to be money paid into Court in accordance with Rule 1 or money paid into Court with a plea of tender (as the case may be), and this Order applies accordingly.
@ref O 14 r 8(2) (src:1393)
GIVEN `the money has been appropriated in accordance with this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `o 14 r 8(2) how the money is appropriated`
GIVETH A MAYBE `o 14 r 8(2) how the appropriated money is deemed to have been paid in`
`o 14 r 8(2) the appropriated money is deemed to be` MEANS
    IF `the money has been appropriated in accordance with this Rule`
    THEN
        CONSIDER way
        WHEN `o 14 r 8(2)(a) by notice to the other party to a particular claim made in the originating claim or counterclaim and specified in the notice` THEN JUST `o 14 r 8(2) money paid into Court in accordance with Rule 1`
        WHEN `o 14 r 8(2)(b) by the party's pleading, as payment into Court of the money alleged to have been tendered` THEN JUST `o 14 r 8(2) money paid into Court with a plea of tender`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "money appropriated in accordance with this Rule"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 14, Rules 9 to 12 -- Exchange Control Act money; payee; small intestate estates; hospital expenses`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1395 | 9. —(1) Where money has been paid into Court in any cause or matter pursuant to the Exchange Control Act, or an order of the Court made under that Act, any party to the cause or matter may apply for payment out of Court of that money. (2) An application for an order under this Rule must be made by summons which must be served on all parties interested.
@ref O 14 r 9(1) (src:1395)
GIVEN `money has been paid into Court in a cause or matter pursuant to the Exchange Control Act or an order of the Court made under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 9(1) any party to the cause or matter may apply for payment out of Court of that money` MEANS
    IF `money has been paid into Court in a cause or matter pursuant to the Exchange Control Act or an order of the Court made under that Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where money has been paid into Court in any cause or matter pursuant to the Exchange Control Act, or an order of the Court made under that Act" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1395 | 9. —(1) Where money has been paid into Court in any cause or matter pursuant to the Exchange Control Act, or an order of the Court made under that Act, any party to the cause or matter may apply for payment out of Court of that money. (2) An application for an order under this Rule must be made by summons which must be served on all parties interested.
@ref O 14 r 9(2) (src:1395)
GIVEN `the application is made by summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons is served on all parties interested` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 9(2) the application is made as required` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by summons` AND `the summons is served on all parties interested`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application for an order under this Rule must be made by summons which must be served on all parties interested" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1396 | (3) If any person in whose favour an order for payment under this Rule is sought is resident outside the scheduled territories as defined in that Act, or will receive payment by order or on behalf of a person so resident, that fact must be stated in the summons.
@ref O 14 r 9(3) (src:1396)
GIVEN `the person in whose favour an order for payment is sought is resident outside the scheduled territories as defined in that Act, or will receive payment by order or on behalf of a person so resident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons states that fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 9(3) the summons states what paragraph (3) requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person in whose favour an order for payment is sought is resident outside the scheduled territories as defined in that Act, or will receive payment by order or on behalf of a person so resident`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- nothing is required where the paragraph's "If" does not hold (fork F-vac in NOTES.md) [marginal-a]
    ELSE
        IF `the summons states that fact`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that fact must be stated in the summons" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1397 | (4) If the permission of the Monetary Authority of Singapore authorising the proposed payment has been given unconditionally or on conditions which have been complied with, that fact must be stated in the summons and the permission must be attached to the summons.
@ref O 14 r 9(4) (src:1397)
GIVEN `the permission of the Monetary Authority of Singapore authorising the proposed payment has been given unconditionally or on conditions which have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons states that fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the permission is attached to the summons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 9(4) the summons states and attaches what paragraph (4) requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the permission of the Monetary Authority of Singapore authorising the proposed payment has been given unconditionally or on conditions which have been complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- nothing is required where the paragraph's "If" does not hold (fork F-vac in NOTES.md) [marginal-a]
    ELSE
        IF `the summons states that fact` AND `the permission is attached to the summons`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that fact must be stated in the summons and the permission must be attached to the summons" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

DECLARE `o 14 r 10 a payee` IS ONE OF
    `o 14 r 10 the party entitled`
    `o 14 r 10 the party's solicitor`
    `o 14 r 10 the Director of Legal Aid`
    `o 14 r 10 any other person`

-- src:1399 | 10. —(1) Where the party entitled to money in Court is a person in respect of whom a certificate is or has been in force entitling him or her to legal aid under the Legal Aid and Advice Act, payment must be made only to that party’s solicitor, or, if he or she is not represented by a solicitor, then, if the Court so orders, to the Director of Legal Aid, without the need for any authority from the party. (2) Subject to paragraph (1), payment must be made to the party entitled or, on his or her written authority, to his or her solicitor or, if the Court so orders, to his or her solicitor without such authority.
@ref O 14 r 10(1) (src:1399)
GIVEN `the party entitled to the money in Court is a person in respect of whom a certificate is or has been in force entitling the person to legal aid under the Legal Aid and Advice Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party is represented by a solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court so orders` IS A BOOLEAN
      payee IS A `o 14 r 10 a payee`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 10(1) payment may be made to this payee` MEANS
    IF `the party entitled to the money in Court is a person in respect of whom a certificate is or has been in force entitling the person to legal aid under the Legal Aid and Advice Act`
    THEN
        CONSIDER payee
        WHEN `o 14 r 10 the party entitled` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "payment must be made only to that party's solicitor, or ... to the Director of Legal Aid"
        WHEN `o 14 r 10 the party's solicitor` THEN
            IF `the party is represented by a solicitor`
            THEN JUST TRUE -- "without the need for any authority from the party"
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the party has no solicitor to receive payment
        WHEN `o 14 r 10 the Director of Legal Aid` THEN
            IF (NOT `the party is represented by a solicitor`) AND `the Court so orders`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if he or she is not represented by a solicitor, then, if the Court so orders, to the Director of Legal Aid" fails
        WHEN `o 14 r 10 any other person` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "payment must be made only to that party's solicitor, or ... to the Director of Legal Aid"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the party entitled to money in Court is a person in respect of whom a certificate is or has been in force"; for any other party paragraph (2) decides

-- src:1399 | 10. —(1) Where the party entitled to money in Court is a person in respect of whom a certificate is or has been in force entitling him or her to legal aid under the Legal Aid and Advice Act, payment must be made only to that party’s solicitor, or, if he or she is not represented by a solicitor, then, if the Court so orders, to the Director of Legal Aid, without the need for any authority from the party. (2) Subject to paragraph (1), payment must be made to the party entitled or, on his or her written authority, to his or her solicitor or, if the Court so orders, to his or her solicitor without such authority.
@ref O 14 r 10(2) (src:1399)
GIVEN `paragraph (1) applies to the party entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party entitled has given written authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court so orders` IS A BOOLEAN
      payee IS A `o 14 r 10 a payee`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 10(2) payment may be made to this payee` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (1) applies to the party entitled`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to paragraph (1)"; paragraph (1) decides
    ELSE
        CONSIDER payee
        WHEN `o 14 r 10 the party entitled` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 14 r 10 the party's solicitor` THEN
            IF `the party entitled has given written authority` OR `the Court so orders`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "payment must be made to the party entitled or, on his or her written authority, to his or her solicitor or, if the Court so orders, to his or her solicitor without such authority"
        WHEN `o 14 r 10 the Director of Legal Aid` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "payment must be made to the party entitled or ... to his or her solicitor"
        WHEN `o 14 r 10 any other person` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "payment must be made to the party entitled or ... to his or her solicitor"

-- src:1400 | (3) This Rule applies whether the money in Court has been paid into Court under Rule 1 or under the order of the Court or a certificate of the Registrar.
@ref O 14 r 10(3) (src:1400)
GIVEN `the money in Court has been paid into Court under Rule 1 or under the order of the Court or a certificate of the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 10(3) this Rule applies to the money` MEANS
    IF `the money in Court has been paid into Court under Rule 1 or under the order of the Court or a certificate of the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "whether the money in Court has been paid into Court under Rule 1 or under the order of the Court or a certificate of the Registrar"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1402 | 11. Where a person entitled to a fund in Court, or a share of such fund, dies intestate and the Court is satisfied that no grant of letters of administration of his or her estate has been made and that the assets of his or her estate do not exceed $50,000 in value, including the value of the fund or share, the Court may order that the fund or share must be paid, transferred or delivered to the person who, being a widower, widow, child, father, mother, brother or sister of the deceased, would have the prior right to a grant of letters of administration of the estate of the deceased.
@ref O 14 r 11 (src:1402)
`o 14 r 11 fifty thousand dollars` MEANS 50000

DECLARE `o 14 r 11 a relative` IS ONE OF
    `o 14 r 11 a widower`
    `o 14 r 11 a widow`
    `o 14 r 11 a child`
    `o 14 r 11 a father`
    `o 14 r 11 a mother`
    `o 14 r 11 a brother`
    `o 14 r 11 a sister`
    `o 14 r 11 any other person`

-- src:1402 | 11. Where a person entitled to a fund in Court, or a share of such fund, dies intestate and the Court is satisfied that no grant of letters of administration of his or her estate has been made and that the assets of his or her estate do not exceed $50,000 in value, including the value of the fund or share, the Court may order that the fund or share must be paid, transferred or delivered to the person who, being a widower, widow, child, father, mother, brother or sister of the deceased, would have the prior right to a grant of letters of administration of the estate of the deceased.
@ref O 14 r 11 (src:1402)
GIVEN `a person entitled to a fund in Court, or a share of such fund, dies intestate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that no grant of letters of administration of the deceased's estate has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the assets of the deceased's estate, including the value of the fund or share` IS A NUMBER
      relative IS A `o 14 r 11 a relative`
      `the person would have the prior right to a grant of letters of administration of the estate of the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 11 the Court may order that the fund or share be paid, transferred or delivered to the person` MEANS
    IF `a person entitled to a fund in Court, or a share of such fund, dies intestate` AND `the Court is satisfied that no grant of letters of administration of the deceased's estate has been made` AND `the value of the assets of the deceased's estate, including the value of the fund or share` AT MOST `o 14 r 11 fifty thousand dollars`
    THEN
        CONSIDER relative
        WHEN `o 14 r 11 a widower` THEN IF `the person would have the prior right to a grant of letters of administration of the estate of the deceased` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who, being a widower, widow, child, father, mother, brother or sister of the deceased, would have the prior right to a grant" [marginal-b]
        WHEN `o 14 r 11 a widow` THEN IF `the person would have the prior right to a grant of letters of administration of the estate of the deceased` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would have the prior right to a grant" [marginal-b]
        WHEN `o 14 r 11 a child` THEN IF `the person would have the prior right to a grant of letters of administration of the estate of the deceased` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would have the prior right to a grant" [marginal-b]
        WHEN `o 14 r 11 a father` THEN IF `the person would have the prior right to a grant of letters of administration of the estate of the deceased` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would have the prior right to a grant" [marginal-b]
        WHEN `o 14 r 11 a mother` THEN IF `the person would have the prior right to a grant of letters of administration of the estate of the deceased` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would have the prior right to a grant" [marginal-b]
        WHEN `o 14 r 11 a brother` THEN IF `the person would have the prior right to a grant of letters of administration of the estate of the deceased` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would have the prior right to a grant" [marginal-b]
        WHEN `o 14 r 11 a sister` THEN IF `the person would have the prior right to a grant of letters of administration of the estate of the deceased` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would have the prior right to a grant" [marginal-b]
        WHEN `o 14 r 11 any other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the order is to "the person who, being a widower, widow, child, father, mother, brother or sister of the deceased"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person entitled to a fund in Court, or a share of such fund, dies intestate and the Court is satisfied that no grant of letters of administration ... has been made and that the assets of his or her estate do not exceed $50,000 in value" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1404 | 12. —(1) This Rule applies in relation to an action or a counterclaim for bodily injury arising out of the use of a motor vehicle on a road or any place to which the public has a right of access in which the claim for damages includes a sum for hospital expenses. (2) Where the party against whom the claim is made, or an approved insurer within the meaning of section 4 of the Motor Vehicles (Third‑Party Risks and Compensation) Act, pays the amount for which that party or insurer (as the case may be) is or may be liable under that Act in respect of the treatment afforded by a hospital to the person in respect of whom the claim is made, the party against whom the claim is made must, within 14 days after payment is made, give notice of the payment to all the other parties to the action.
@ref O 14 r 12(1) (src:1404)
GIVEN `it is an action or a counterclaim for bodily injury arising out of the use of a motor vehicle on a road or any place to which the public has a right of access` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim for damages includes a sum for hospital expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 12(1) this Rule applies in relation to the action or counterclaim` MEANS
    IF `it is an action or a counterclaim for bodily injury arising out of the use of a motor vehicle on a road or any place to which the public has a right of access` AND `the claim for damages includes a sum for hospital expenses`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an action or a counterclaim for bodily injury arising out of the use of a motor vehicle ... in which the claim for damages includes a sum for hospital expenses"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1404 | 12. —(1) This Rule applies in relation to an action or a counterclaim for bodily injury arising out of the use of a motor vehicle on a road or any place to which the public has a right of access in which the claim for damages includes a sum for hospital expenses. (2) Where the party against whom the claim is made, or an approved insurer within the meaning of section 4 of the Motor Vehicles (Third‑Party Risks and Compensation) Act, pays the amount for which that party or insurer (as the case may be) is or may be liable under that Act in respect of the treatment afforded by a hospital to the person in respect of whom the claim is made, the party against whom the claim is made must, within 14 days after payment is made, give notice of the payment to all the other parties to the action.
@ref O 14 r 12(2) (src:1404)
`o 14 r 12(2) fourteen days after payment is made` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:1404 | 12. —(1) This Rule applies in relation to an action or a counterclaim for bodily injury arising out of the use of a motor vehicle on a road or any place to which the public has a right of access in which the claim for damages includes a sum for hospital expenses. (2) Where the party against whom the claim is made, or an approved insurer within the meaning of section 4 of the Motor Vehicles (Third‑Party Risks and Compensation) Act, pays the amount for which that party or insurer (as the case may be) is or may be liable under that Act in respect of the treatment afforded by a hospital to the person in respect of whom the claim is made, the party against whom the claim is made must, within 14 days after payment is made, give notice of the payment to all the other parties to the action.
@ref O 14 r 12(2) (src:1404)
GIVEN `this Rule applies in relation to the action or counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party against whom the claim is made, or an approved insurer within the meaning of section 4 of the Motor Vehicles (Third-Party Risks and Compensation) Act, pays the amount for which that party or insurer is or may be liable under that Act in respect of the treatment afforded by a hospital to the person in respect of whom the claim is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 12(2) the party against whom the claim is made must give notice of the payment to all the other parties` MEANS
    IF `this Rule applies in relation to the action or counterclaim` AND `the party against whom the claim is made, or an approved insurer within the meaning of section 4 of the Motor Vehicles (Third-Party Risks and Compensation) Act, pays the amount for which that party or insurer is or may be liable under that Act in respect of the treatment afforded by a hospital to the person in respect of whom the claim is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the party against whom the claim is made, or an approved insurer ..., pays the amount for which that party or insurer ... is or may be liable under that Act in respect of the treatment afforded by a hospital" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1404 | 12. —(1) This Rule applies in relation to an action or a counterclaim for bodily injury arising out of the use of a motor vehicle on a road or any place to which the public has a right of access in which the claim for damages includes a sum for hospital expenses. (2) Where the party against whom the claim is made, or an approved insurer within the meaning of section 4 of the Motor Vehicles (Third‑Party Risks and Compensation) Act, pays the amount for which that party or insurer (as the case may be) is or may be liable under that Act in respect of the treatment afforded by a hospital to the person in respect of whom the claim is made, the party against whom the claim is made must, within 14 days after payment is made, give notice of the payment to all the other parties to the action.
@ref O 14 r 12(2) (src:1404)
GIVEN `the date the party gives notice of the payment to all the other parties to the action` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 14 r 12(2) the party gives notice of the payment in time` MEANS
    IF `the date the party gives notice of the payment to all the other parties to the action` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after payment is made, give notice of the payment to all the other parties to the action" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05, (a))

DECLARE `o 14 r 12(2) party` IS ONE OF
    `o 14 r 12(2) the party against whom the claim is made`

DECLARE `o 14 r 12(2) act` IS ONE OF
